ntically identical (16/16), gating correct, no-op pin\n80\t  non-vacuous â†’ GO.\n81\t- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** prompt caching is a **no-op for Aurora's current prompt sizes** â€”\n82\t  all roles' stable prefixes are 15â€“60Ã— below the model minimum. The plumbing is correct and\n83\t  gated; it activates automatically only if a role's stable prefix ever exceeds the minimum. This\n84\t  refines the AuroraTwo research's #1 \"cheap win\" (it was corroboration-only; measured as\n85\t  inapplicable at current sizes). No cost savings banked.\n86\t\n87\t### Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n88\t\n89\t- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `output_schema` via strict forced\n90\t  tool-use (`emit_result` tool whose input_schema IS the caller schema; SDK has no metering-safe\n91\t  native parse path); shared `CRITIC_VERDICT_SCHEMA`/`RECONCILED_VERDICT_SCHEMA` in contracts.py +\n92\t  `JUDGE_DECISION_SCHEMA`; critic_a/critic_b(Anthropic-fallback)/reconciler/judge pass schemas;\n93\t  Gemini path + langextract untouched. Off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed, enforced by\n94\t  `_parse_response`, not by `strict`).\n95\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 874 passed (869 after EXECUTE, +5 after FIX). No test weakening.\n96\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (fail-closed independently re-verified by the\n97\t  parser). R2 GO-conditional with W5-F1 (MEDIUM): no-`required` strict schema acceptance is\n98\t  unverified against the live API; a rejection would 400 on both Sonnet+Haiku and (since\n99\t  critic/reconciler weren't exception-wrapped) abort the nightly sweep. FIX iter 1: structured call\n100\t  now DEGRADES to a plain text call on any structured-call failure (metered once off the successful\n101\t  call, degrade logged) + defense-in-depth (critic_a/b/reconciler treat a hard call error as\n102\t  degrade-to-None). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n103\t- **TRIPWIRE:** if the live API rejects the no-`required` strict schema, structured outputs silently\n104\t  degrade to the legacy plain-text parse (no benefit, no harm). A one-call live smoke against\n105\t  Sonnet/Haiku would confirm whether the schema activates; until then, treat L3 as best-effort.\n106\t\n107\t### Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n108\t\n109\t- **Deliverables:** `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `effort` (maps to `thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}`\n110\t  + `output_config={\"effort\": low|medium|high|xhigh|max}` per the claude-api skill); a recursive\n111\t  `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard runs before EVERY Anthropic dispatch (initial + Haiku fallback +\n112\t  structuredâ†’plain degrade) â€” Opus 4.8 400s on budget_tokens; `_fold_thinking_into_output` folds any\n113\t  separately-reported thinking tokens into metered output (the $118 lesson). Default (effort unset) =\n114\t  cost-neutral, byte-for-byte unchanged. Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard + `thoughts_token_count`\n115\t  fold untouched.\n116\t- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 891 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n117\t- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Guard verified comprehensive + recursive (catches nested\n118\t  budget_tokens); fold matches Anthropic's real usage semantics (thinking already in output_tokens â†’\n119\t  fold is a correct no-op today, no double-count); mutation-resistant tests (fold-removal under-meter\n120\t  AND double-count over-meter both caught).\n121\t- **TRIPWIRES (LOW, latent, opt-in path only):** (1) the additive thinking-fold could *over*-meter if\n122\t  a future Anthropic usage field duplicates already-counted thinking tokens â€” no current field exists,\n123\t  forward-compat bet; (2) `effort=max`/`xhigh` on a non-Opus model passes Aurora's validation but\n124\t  would 400 live (intentional; harmless while effort is default-unset and unwired by roles).\n125\t\n126\t### Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + tokenizer factor â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n127\t\n