ild).\n\n### Wave 4 â€” L2: Prompt caching â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `cache_system` (structured\n  ephemeral system block, cache-read/write metered via L1); invariant rubric/schema moved into the\n  cached system block for critic_a, reconciler, security judge; Sonnetâ†’Haiku fallback carries the\n  marker; default (cache-off) path byte-for-byte unchanged.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 858 passed (854 after EXECUTE, +4 after FIX). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers. R1 GO (default unchanged, fallback caches, the 3 modified test mocks are\n  faithful signature propagation not weakening). R2 GO with a HIGH efficacy finding (W4-R2-1):\n  cached prefixes (65â€“317 tok) are far below Anthropic's per-model minimums (Sonnet 2048 / Haiku\n  4096), so caching silently never fires. FIX iter 1: maximized the stable prefix (moved invariant\n  rubric/schema into system â€” token-multiset identical, F6 fences intact), then GATED the marker\n  behind `cache_prefix_clears_minimum` (no dead marker sent) and added honesty-pinning tests.\n  Closure VERIFIER: judge content semantically identical (16/16), gating correct, no-op pin\n  non-vacuous â†’ GO.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** prompt caching is a **no-op for Aurora's current prompt sizes** â€”\n  all roles' stable prefixes are 15â€“60Ã— below the model minimum. The plumbing is correct and\n  gated; it activates automatically only if a role's stable prefix ever exceeds the minimum. This\n  refines the AuroraTwo research's #1 \"cheap win\" (it was corroboration-only; measured as\n  inapplicable at current sizes). No cost savings banked.\n\n### Wave 5 â€” L3: Structured outputs â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `output_schema` via strict forced\n  tool-use (`emit_result` tool whose input_schema IS the caller schema; SDK has no metering-safe\n  native parse path); shared `CRITIC_VERDICT_SCHEMA`/`RECONCILED_VERDICT_SCHEMA` in contracts.py +\n  `JUDGE_DECISION_SCHEMA`; critic_a/critic_b(Anthropic-fallback)/reconciler/judge pass schemas;\n  Gemini path + langextract untouched. Off-schema judge â†’ abstain (fail-closed, enforced by\n  `_parse_response`, not by `strict`).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 874 passed (869 after EXECUTE, +5 after FIX). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (fail-closed independently re-verified by the\n  parser). R2 GO-conditional with W5-F1 (MEDIUM): no-`required` strict schema acceptance is\n  unverified against the live API; a rejection would 400 on both Sonnet+Haiku and (since\n  critic/reconciler weren't exception-wrapped) abort the nightly sweep. FIX iter 1: structured call\n  now DEGRADES to a plain text call on any structured-call failure (metered once off the successful\n  call, degrade logged) + defense-in-depth (critic_a/b/reconciler treat a hard call error as\n  degrade-to-None). Closure VERIFIER mutation-tested all â†’ GO.\n- **TRIPWIRE:** if the live API rejects the no-`required` strict schema, structured outputs silently\n  degrade to the legacy plain-text parse (no benefit, no harm). A one-call live smoke against\n  Sonnet/Haiku would confirm whether the schema activates; until then, treat L3 as best-effort.\n\n### Wave 6 â€” L4: Adaptive thinking via `effort` â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `call_anthropic`/`call_model` gain `effort` (maps to `thinking={\"type\":\"adaptive\"}`\n  + `output_config={\"effort\": low|medium|high|xhigh|max}` per the claude-api skill); a recursive\n  `_assert_no_budget_tokens` guard runs before EVERY Anthropic dispatch (initial + Haiku fallback +\n  structuredâ†’plain degrade) â€” Opus 4.8 400s on budget_tokens; `_fold_thinking_into_output` folds any\n  separately-reported thinking tokens into metered output (the $118 lesson). Default (effort unset) =\n  cost-neutral, byte-for-byte unchanged. Gemini `thinking_budget=0` guard + `thoughts_token_count`\n  fold untouched.\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 891 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Guard verified comprehensive + recursive (catches nested\n  budget_tokens); fold matches Anthropic's real usage semantics (thinking already in output_tokens â†’\n  fold is a correct no-op today, no double-count); mutation-resistant tests (fold-removal under-meter\n  AND double-count over-meter both caught).\n- **TRIPWIRES (LOW, latent, opt-in path only):** (1) the additive thinking-fold could *over*-meter if\n  a future Anthropic usage field duplicates already-counted thinking tokens â€” no current field exists,\n  forward-compat bet; (2) `effort=max`/`xhigh` on a non-Opus model passes Aurora's validation but\n  would 400 live (intentional; harmless while effort is default-unset and unwired by roles).\n\n### Wave 7 â€” L5: Model retargeting + tokenizer factor â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `kb/pricing.yaml` adds `claude-opus-4-8` ($5/$25, verified:true) with L1-style\n  cache sub-rates + `tokenizer_factor: 1.35` (verified:false); `llm.py` `tokenizer_factor`/\n  `estimate_tokens`/`estimate_usd` estimate-only helpers (factor NEVER touches post-call metering â€”\n  ground-truth invariant, regression-pinned).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 898 passed (+7). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. R1 nothing found (post-call metering provably unfactored;\n  mutation-proven ground-truth test). R2 GO with **honesty findings**: (F1, HIGH-honesty) the\n  estimate helpers are **dead code** â€” no production caller (Aurora budgets in fixed-USD, not token\n  pre-flight), so the tokenizer-factor accuracy goal is not realized; (F2) the defaults were ALREADY\n  on current tiers, so \"retargeting\" changed nothing in the default path. Same inert-plumbing\n  pattern as L2 caching. Corrected an overstated orchestrator comment (F2b).\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** L5's concrete value is narrow â€” `claude-opus-4-8` is now priced so\n  an `AURORA_*_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8` override meters correctly instead of $0 (closes a $0-fiction\n  hole on the Opus override path) + a deprecated-Opus guard test. The tokenizer factor + estimate\n  helpers are correct, tested, forward-ready, but **inert until a token-budget pre-flight consumer\n  exists**. (F3, LOW: a future 4.7+ model added without the field silently estimates at 1.0.)\n\n### Wave 8 â€” L6: Message Batches API â€” GREEN (2026-06-07)\n\n- **Deliverables:** `llm.py` `submit_anthropic_batch` + poll/collect + `build_anthropic_request_params`\n  (params identical to the synchronous shape incl. L2 cache / L3 tools / L4 effort + budget_tokens\n  guard) + `_meter_batch_result` (records each result `batch_mode=True` â†’ L1's 0.5Ã— from real usage);\n  `roles/batch_sweep.py` opt-in coordinator (`AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP`, default off); critic_a/reconciler\n  refactored into `build_prompt`/`parse_verdict` + a `prefetched_text` param; orchestrator batches\n  critic_a behind the flag. Per-item failure / timeout / missing result â†’ synchronous degrade\n  (`batch_mode=False`, `_note_degrade`); missing security-judge result â†’ abstain (fail-closed).\n- **Gate:** `python -m pytest` = 915 passed (+17). No test weakening.\n- **Review:** 2 reviewers, both GO. Flag-off path verified byte-for-byte (git-diff-confirmed the\n  critic_a/reconciler parse extraction is verbatim; equivalence also guarded by existing\n  test_structured_outputs + test_critic_c); batch metered exactly 0.5Ã—; per-item degrade + ~65-min\n  poll-timeout-degrade + judge fail-closed all tested; budget_tokens guard runs on batch params.\n- **HONEST OUTCOME / TRIPWIRE:** like L2/L5, this is **ready plumbing, not a current win**. Only\n  critic_a is wired (1 of 3 per-candidate Anthropic calls, â‰¤400 tokens); reconciler-batch +\n  judge-batch are built+tested but unwired (reconciler has a hard data-dependency on critic output;\n  judge is on the separate gate path). At TOP_K=2 that's ~2 small calls/night â†’ sub-cent savings, and\n  the blocking poll (up to ~65 min) makes `AURORA_BATCH_SWEEP=1` **net-negative EV at current scale**.\n  Default-off is correct; revisit only if TOP_K rises substantially.\n\n---\n\n## Phase 2 â€” PROJECT DONE â€” 2026-06-07\n\nAll 8 planned waves built EXECUTE â†’ ADVERSARIAL-REVIEW (2 independent reviewers) â†’ FIX â†’ RE-REVIEW\nand converged GREEN, in order, on branch `foreman/aurora-revamp`.\n\n- **Security thread (Wave 1-2, live verdict path):** H1 payload-depth scan (monotonic, honest\n  scan-depth labeling) + H2 evidence-loop promotion machinery (default-legacy, nightly zero-cost,\n  $0-shadowâ†’NO-GO gate, adoption monotonic-toward-stricter). Both real value.\n- **llm.py thread (Wave 3-8):** L1 cost substrate (real, enabling) Â· L3 structured outputs (real\n  robustness + safe degrade) Â· L4 budget_tokens guard + thinking fold (real â€” prevents Opus 4.8 400s,\n  guards the $118 class). **L2 caching / L5 retarget / L6 batch are correct, honest, forward-ready\n  PLUMBING that is largely INERT at Aurora's current prompt sizes + TOP_K=2** â€” exactly the research's\n  \"validate before banking\" caveat, now measured.\n- **Ground-truth gate:** `python -m pytest` = **915 passed** (+163 across the 8 waves from the 752\n  Phase-1 baseline). No test weakening anywhere; security suite green throughout.\n- **Locked-preserved intact:** KB schema + library, single-owner security gate, deterministic cost\n  telemetry (post-call metering never altered by any wave), Helping Hand + publisher.\n- **SEPARATELY-AUTHORIZED, NOT run:** H2 SA-1 (metered shadow batch) + SA-2 (live evidence-engine\n  flip); the live H1 payload re-stamp against kb/aurora.db. All gated, default-off.\n- **Commits:** 0eca5f2 (W1) Â· ffae677 (W2) Â· 2618f59 (W3) Â· 0a24914 (W4) Â· f046810 (W5) Â· e604fa4\n  (W6) Â· 7b23c9e (W7) Â· + W8. Not pushed; awaiting John's review.\n","numLines":189,"startLine":1,"totalLines":189}}}
